WEBVTT

00:39:27.646 --> 00:39:30.255
This is, in a way, a bit of pushback.

00:39:30.279 --> 00:39:31.568
SC: Yeah. Yep. Sure.

00:39:31.592 --> 00:39:34.854
CA: Actually, this article credits you --
or blames you, perhaps --

00:39:34.878 --> 00:39:40.085
with the fact that the internet
is now overwhelmed with memes

00:39:40.109 --> 00:39:42.538
that basically celebrate introverts.

00:39:42.562 --> 00:39:46.086
And I think the author's saying extroverts
are starting to get a hard deal.

00:39:46.110 --> 00:39:47.841
And there's this line in here:

00:39:47.865 --> 00:39:52.117
"Introversion has been romanticized
into an image of a thoughtful soul

00:39:52.141 --> 00:39:54.284
wandering through nature, book in hand,

00:39:54.308 --> 00:39:56.429
considering life's big picture.

00:39:56.453 --> 00:39:59.834
Extroversion, meanwhile, is a boorish
individual at a loud party,

00:39:59.858 --> 00:40:02.549
demanding attention and holding
forth in a conversation